Howdy,

Since making the unfortunate discovery that, yes, nethack is available
for my iPhone, I've been playing on and off for a few months after
many years of successful abstinence.

To be specific, I'm playing Slash'EM, the one that has the Enforcer
patch compiled in.  It's not entirely stable - seems to have some
issues with maintaining the inventory, and sometimes advises you that
you should quit (!) due to 'program in disarry' - but the interface
works for me.

Anyway, I like the enforcer class, in part because there's so little
specific spoilage available for it.  My latest hobbit enforcer was, I
thought, well on his way to Ascension, having done Grund's, Mine's
End, and the Lawful Quest, mostly on the strenght of Excalibur, and
despite having a desperately high armor class for most of it.  I'd
consolidated some, finally got a robe of protection (very burnt, but
still) off the mind flayers in the Lawful Quest, a respectable AC of
-13, though I really needed a cloak of magic resistance or protection.

Venturing down a little farther, I found a magic portal on level 17.
Hmmm...  OK, let's pop in and see what it is...  Pop!  Oh, look, I'm
surrounded by V's, L's, and Z's!  This doesn't seem good.  Where's the
portal?  I'm going to die, aren't I?

So, yeah, it was the Chaotic Quest, and it seems like it had set me
down in some very large room with Vecna standing on the portal.  My
first two actions were to take a step towards what I thought was the
corner of the room - it wasn't, and I never actually saw anything that
indicated a wall (my ring of warning made it look like I was in a
bigroom), and to swap on my ring of conflict.  Then I engaged my
enforcer blink.  At that point I think something hit me with a potion
of paralyzation and I went from ~120 HP to 11 before I got another
action.  I drank my potion of full healing and burned Elbereth with my
wand of fire.  I then used Nighthorn to heal my strength back from 9
to 18 - not even sure what had drained it and regain my full HP.

Meanwhile the entire room was filling with master lich summoned
monsters, including a captain (an @) and a master mind flayer.  I
seemed to be safe, relatively, and even managed to stop the portal as
things moved about, but it was two moves away diagonally, which there
was no way in hell I was going to make without dying.  Around this
point, though, something went terribly wrong, and I'm not even sure
what it was.  I don't remember the precise order of things:

 - I tried zapping my wand of undead turning to clear a path towards
the portal, and did blow up an orc zombie or similar, but the mind
flayer filled in the gap before I could take a step.
 - The captain had started beating on me, but I was just ignoring him.
 - I swapped my ring of warning for a ring of regeneration.
 - I tried to zap my wand of fire at Vecna, but it was out of charges.

Suddenly I started taking attacks from all sides, as if the Elbereth
had been broken.  I think I got in one action between having >80 HP
and being dead.  >>> Did zapping the wands damage the Elbereth?  I
read and reread the Elbereth spoilers, and they seemed to indicate
that only melee combat would mess up the Elbereth.  Or did the
captain's unanswered attacks on me mess it up? <<<

Anyway, I don't know that there's anything I could've done to survive,
though having re-reread the Elbereth spoiler it seems clear that I
should've put on my amulet of flying and hovered over Elbereth; the
Chaotic Quest seems to me to have been instakill for anything not
ready for Ascension in this instance.  The spoilers make it sound like
it's not meant to be quite so devastating in general, but I'm not sure
I'll be stepping on any portals between levels 15 and 19 in the future
until I've genocided L.

Bargle,
